ol levels exceeding 500 mg/dl. Due to its implications for cardiovascular health, Hipercolesterolemia Familiar is a major focus of research within the field of endocrinology, as it often leads to serious cardiovascular events.", "CELULAS MESENQUIMALES:Mesenchymal cells are a focus of research in diabetes treatment, particularly in relation to type 1 diabetes.", "PROYECTOS DE INVESTIGACIÓN:Research projects related to diabetes are a key aspect of Samuel Namara's work as a principal investigator.", "JUNTA DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE ENDOCRINOLOGÍA Y NUTRICIÓN:The board of the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition oversees educational programs for residents and continuing education for specialists.", "GRUPOS DE TRABAJO DE DIABETES:Working groups on diabetes within the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition focus on advancing knowledge and treatment of diabetes.", "GRUPO DE CONSENSOS DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE DIABETES:A consensus group within the Spanish Diabetes Society that works on guidelines and best practices for diabetes management.", "GRUPO DE LÍPIDOS DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE ENDOCRINOLOGÍA Y NUTRICIÓN:A working group focused on lipid disorders within the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition.", "HIPERCOLESTEROLEMIA POLIGÉNICA:Hipercolesterolemia poligénica is a common condition characterized by moderate levels of cholesterol in the plasma, typically ranging between 240 and 350 mg/dl. This condition arises from the interaction of multiple genetic factors and environmental influences, leading to elevated cholesterol levels.", "DEFICIT FAMILIAR DE APOPROTEÍNA B-100:Este trastorno autosómico dominante es una fenocopia de la hipercolesterolemia familiar, causado por una mutación que afecta la afinidad de la LDL por su receptor.", "EZETIMIBA:Ezetimiba is a medication that can be added to statins to help achieve LDL cholesterol goals. It works by inhibiting the absorption of cholesterol and phytosterols in the intestine, making it primarily effective in lowering LDL cholesterol levels.", "INHIBIDORES DE PCSK9:Los inhibidores de PCSK9 son una clase de medicamentos que ayudan a reducir los niveles de colesterol LDL en pacientes que no logran el control adecuado con estatinas.", "ALIROCUMAB:Alirocumab es un inhibidor de PCSK9 utilizado para el tratamiento de la hipercolesterolemia.", "SENSIBILIDAD A LA INSULINA:La sensibilidad a la insulina se refiere a la capacidad del cuerpo para responder a la insulina, y su disminución está relacionada con la dislipidemia aterogénica."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}